    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Compassionate release - the release of incarcerated people with medical conditions from\r\nprisons and jails - is a widely underutilized mechanism. Releasing people with medical\r\nconditions from carceral settings can protect individuals’ health - especially during crises such as\r\nthe COVID-19 pandemic - and can help promote the health of all people experiencing\r\nincarceration by reducing overcrowding. More literature is needed to understand the barriers and\r\nfacilitators to compassionate release to encourage its utilization. The first section of this thesis is\r\na scoping review that maps existing literature on compassionate release to Bronfenbrenner’s\r\nEcological Systems Theory to understand key recommendations for improving compassionate\r\nrelease and where there are gaps in the literature. Findings from this review demonstrate key\r\nrecommendations such as establishing greater transparency in the application process, ensuring\r\naccessibility of applications based on literacy levels, and establishing medical-legal partnerships.\r\nIdentified gaps for future research include understanding racial disparities in compassionate\r\nrelease as well as understanding perspectives of caregivers of previously incarcerated\r\nindividuals. The second section of this thesis presents a survey study on perceptions towards\r\ncompassionate release from jail staff in California during the COVID-19 pandemic. Results\r\nhighlight that not all jails in California use compassionate release widely and compassionate\r\nrelease remains inaccessible for people such as those with respiratory illnesses and people\r\nconvicted of violent crimes. Engaging carceral staff using evidence-based recommendations is\r\ncrucial in expanding compassionate release. Implementing these recommendations and\r\nresearching identified gaps can inform policy and practice to promote the health of people\r\nexperiencing incarceration.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "King, Z. (2022). Searching for Compassion in Compassionate Release: Protecting the Health of People Experiencing Incarceration. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/mm543jr6552. https://doi.org/10.25740/mm543jr6552.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
